{
  "tabs": [
    {
      "name": "Core",
      "rows": [
        {
          "forceHeight": "64px",
          "components": [
            {
              "field": "type",
              "name": "Layer Type",
              "description": "",
              "type": "dropdown",
              "width": 2,
              "options": [
                "data",
                "header",
                "image",
                "model",
                "query",
                "tile",
                "vector",
                "vectortile",
                "velocity",
                "video"
              ]
            },
            {
              "field": "name",
              "name": "Layer Name",
              "description": "",
              "type": "textnotrim",
              "width": 8,
              "required": true
            },
            {
              "field": "visibility",
              "name": "Initially On",
              "description": "",
              "type": "checkbox",
              "width": 2,
              "defaultChecked": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Data Tiles",
          "components": [
            {
              "field": "demSourceType",
              "name": "Source Type",
              "description": "What the 'Data Tile URL' is meant to reference. See the 'Data Tile URL' description for more.",
              "type": "dropdown",
              "width": 2,
              "options": ["url", "COG", "stac-collection"]
            },
            {
              "field": "demtileurl",
              "name": "Data Tile URL",
              "description": "<strong>• URL: '{url}'</strong> A path to a tileset of RGBA-encoded float32 PNG tiles, typically generated by MMGIS auxiliary scripts (rasterstotiles1bto4b.py). Each pixel stores a 32-bit float as big-endian IEEE 754 RGBA bytes. If the path is relative, it is relative to the Missions/{mission} directory. Append /{z}/{x}/{y}.png to your URL.\n\t<strong>• COG: 'COG:{path_or_url_to_cog.tif}'</strong> A path or URL to a single-band Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF. MMGIS fetches float32 tiles from TiTiler and decodes them client-side. A relative path is served from the Missions/{mission} directory. TiTiler must be enabled. Example: COG:/Missions/MyMission/Data/elevation.tif\n\t<strong>• STAC-COLLECTION (Local): 'stac-collection:{collection_name}'</strong> A STAC collection hosted by this MMGIS instance's titiler-pgstac. Tiles are mosaicked COGs from the collection. titiler-pgstac must be enabled. Example: stac-collection:my_elevation_collection\n\t<strong>• STAC-COLLECTION (External): 'stac-collection:https://other-mmgis.com/titilerpgstac/collections/{collection_name}'</strong> A STAC collection from an external MMGIS instance. The external server must have CORS enabled and titiler-pgstac available.",
              "type": "text",
              "width": 8,
              "required": true
            },
            {
              "field": "demparser",
              "name": "DEM Parser",
              "description": "<strong>• npy (default for COG/STAC)</strong> NumPy binary tiles (.npy) from TiTiler — raw float32, no compression, fastest for full float32 precision.\\n\\t<strong>• terrarium</strong> Mapzen Terrarium-encoded PNG tiles (.png?algorithm=terrarium) — elevation = R×256 + G + B÷256 − 32768. Smaller files (~10–50 KB/tile) with ~1 cm precision; faster network transfer.\\n\\t<strong>• terrainrgb</strong> Mapbox TerrainRGB-encoded PNG tiles (.png?algorithm=terrainrgb) — elevation = −10000 + (R×65536 + G×256 + B)×0.1. Smaller files with ~0.1 m precision.\\n\\t<strong>• rgba (url source only)</strong> RGBA-encoded float32 PNG tiles generated by MMGIS auxiliary scripts.\\n\\t<strong>• tif (url source only)</strong> GeoTIFF tiles.",
              "type": "dropdown",
              "width": 2,
              "options": ["npy", "terrarium", "terrainrgb", "rgba", "tif"]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "field": "tileformat",
              "name": "Tile Format",
              "description": "",
              "type": "dropdown",
              "width": 7,
              "options": ["tms", "wmts", "wms"]
            },
            {
              "field": "controlled",
              "name": "Controlled",
              "description": "",
              "type": "checkbox",
              "width": 2,
              "defaultChecked": false
            },
            {
              "field": "initialOpacity",
              "name": "Initial Opacity",
              "description": "0 (transparent) to 1 (opaque)",
              "type": "number",
              "min": 0,
              "width": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "field": "minZoom",
              "name": "Minimum Zoom",
              "description": "",
              "type": "number",
              "min": 0,
              "step": 1,
              "width": 3,
              "required": true
            },
            {
              "field": "maxNativeZoom",
              "name": "Maximum Native Zoom",
              "description": "",
              "type": "number",
              "min": 0,
              "step": 1,
              "width": 2,
              "required": true
            },
            {
              "field": "maxZoom",
              "name": "Maximum Zoom",
              "description": "",
              "type": "number",
              "min": 0,
              "step": 1,
              "width": 3,
              "required": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Other",
          "components": [
            {
              "field": "boundingBox",
              "name": "Bounding Box",
              "description": "minx,miny,maxx,maxy",
              "type": "textarray",
              "width": 12
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Actions",
          "components": [
            {
              "name": "Populate Fields From tilemapresource.xml or from cog/info",
              "description": "If the above URL is relative to the Missions/{mission} directory and the tileset contains a tilemapresource.xml within it, queries that xml and auto-fills the 'Minimum Zoom', 'Maximum Native Zoom' and 'Bounding Box' fields above. If it is a COG and TiTiler is true, the COG's data will be queried instead.",
              "type": "button",
              "action": "tile-populate-from-x",
              "width": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
